---
// "Try it yourself": three reflection exercises readers can fill in –
// introducing themselves as their mother would, drawing the mountain of
// their life, and listing their values. Everything stays in the reader's
// browser (saved in localStorage on this device only); nothing is sent.
---

<section class="kit" aria-labelledby="kit-title" data-kit>
  <header class="kit-head">
    <p class="kit-label">Try it yourself</p>
    <h2 id="kit-title" class="kit-title">
      Your own reflection
    </h2>
    <p class="kit-intro">
      Three short exercises from the session: introduce yourself through your
      mother's eyes, draw the mountain of your life, and name your values.
    </p>
    <p class="kit-privacy">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true">
        <path
          d="M12 2 4 5v6c0 5 3.4 9.4 8 11 4.6-1.6 8-6 8-11V5l-8-3Z"
          fill="currentColor"
        ></path>
      </svg>
      Private: what you write stays on this device. Nothing is sent or stored on
      this website.
    </p>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="solid kit-open"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="kit-body"
      data-open
    >
      <span data-open-label>Open the exercises</span>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true">
        <path
          d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2.2"
        ></path>
      </svg>
    </button>
  </header>

  <div id="kit-body" class="kit-body" hidden data-body>
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Exercises">
      <button role="tab" id="kt-1" aria-controls="kp-1" aria-selected="true">
        <span>1</span> Through your mother's eyes
      </button>
      <button
        role="tab"
        id="kt-2"
        aria-controls="kp-2"
        aria-selected="false"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <span>2</span> Your mountain
      </button>
      <button
        role="tab"
        id="kt-3"
        aria-controls="kp-3"
        aria-selected="false"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <span>3</span> Your values
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Mother's point of view -->
    <div role="tabpanel" id="kp-1" aria-labelledby="kt-1" class="panel">
      <p class="how">
        Imagine your mother – or the mother figure in your life – introducing
        you to a room of strangers. Answer as her.
      </p>
      <div class="fields">
        <label>
          Your name{" "}
          <input
            data-k="m.name"
            type="text"
            autocomplete="off"
            placeholder="So she can introduce you"
          />
        </label>
        <label>
          What of me is in them?{" "}
          <textarea
            data-k="m.mine"
            rows="2"
            placeholder="My stubbornness, my love of music…"
          ></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          What am I proud of? <textarea data-k="m.proud" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          What do I hope for their future?{" "}
          <textarea data-k="m.hope" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          One thing I got wrong in raising them – and am sorry for{" "}
          <textarea data-k="m.sorry" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="out" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="out-label">Her introduction</p>
        <p class="intro-text" data-out="intro">
          Start typing, and her introduction will appear here.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="prompt">
        <b>Reflect:</b> what did writing in her voice show you about yourself as
        a leader?
      </p>
      <textarea
        data-k="m.reflect"
        rows="3"
        aria-label="Your reflection on the introduction"
      ></textarea>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. Mountain -->
    <div role="tabpanel" id="kp-2" aria-labelledby="kt-2" class="panel" hidden>
      <p class="how">
        Divide your life into stages, from birth to today. For each, give it a
        name and say how high or low it felt. Then mark the moments that shaped
        the climb.
      </p>
      <div class="stages" data-stages></div>
      <button type="button" class="ghost" data-add-stage>
        + Add a stage
      </button>

      <figure class="mtn">
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 720 340"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Your mountain of life"
          data-mtn
        ></svg>
      </figure>

      <div class="fields two">
        <label>
          When I was held up – by whom, and how{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.held" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          My lowest point – and why{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.low" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          A risk I took that mattered{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.risk" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          When I felt on top of the world{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.peak" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          A time I gave in to pressure{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.pressure" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          A contradiction I still find hard to live with{" "}
          <textarea data-k="t.contra" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
      </div>
      <label class="wide">
        At C5, today: one sentence about what I see for myself next
        <textarea data-k="t.next" rows="2"></textarea>
      </label>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. Values -->
    <div role="tabpanel" id="kp-3" aria-labelledby="kt-3" class="panel" hidden>
      <p class="how">
        A value is what you are willing to pay a price for. List up to six
        values you hold. For each, be honest: have you paid a price for it?
      </p>
      <div class="values" data-values></div>
      <button type="button" class="ghost" data-add-value>
        + Add a value
      </button>

      <div class="out" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="out-label">Your values at a glance</p>
        <div data-out="values" class="chips">
          <span class="muted">Your values will appear here.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fields">
        <label>
          A "dirty" value I act on but would rather not admit{" "}
          <textarea
            data-k="v.dirty"
            rows="2"
            placeholder="The need for approval, the fear of conflict…"
          ></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          Who were my biggest value influencers?{" "}
          <textarea data-k="v.influencers" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label>
          One value I will start paying a price for{" "}
          <textarea data-k="v.commit" rows="2"></textarea>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="kit-foot">
      <button type="button" class="solid" data-print>
        Save my reflection as PDF
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="ghost" data-clear>
        Clear everything
      </button>
    </footer>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-kit]");
  if (root) init(root);

  type Stage = { name: string; h: number };
  type Value = { name: string; paid: string; note: string };
  type State = {
    f: Record<string, string>;
    stages: Stage[];
    values: Value[];
  };

  function init(root: HTMLElement) {
    const body = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-body]")!;
    const openBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-open]")!;
    const openLabel = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-open-label]")!;
    openBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const open = body.hidden;
      body.hidden = !open;
      openBtn.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open));
      openLabel.textContent = open
        ? "Close the exercises"
        : "Open the exercises";
      if (open) drawMountain();
    });
    const KEY = "fpa-reflection-kit-v1";
    const blank = (): State => ({
      f: {},
      stages: [
        { name: "Childhood", h: 5 },
        { name: "", h: 5 },
        { name: "", h: 5 },
        { name: "", h: 5 },
        { name: "Today", h: 6 },
      ],
      values: [
        { name: "", paid: "", note: "" },
        { name: "", paid: "", note: "" },
        { name: "", paid: "", note: "" },
      ],
    });

    let state: State = blank();
    try {
      const saved = localStorage.getItem(KEY);
      if (saved) state = { ...blank(), ...JSON.parse(saved) };
    } catch {
      /* storage unavailable: the tool still works for this visit */
    }
    const save = () => {
      try {
        localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(state));
      } catch {
        /* ignore */
      }
    };

    const esc = (s: string) =>
      s.replace(
        /[&<>"]/g,
        (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;" })[c]!,
      );

    // ---------- tabs ----------
    const tabs = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
    const select = (i: number) => {
      tabs.forEach((t, j) => {
        const on = i === j;
        t.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(on));
        t.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
        root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(
          "#" + t.getAttribute("aria-controls"),
        )!.hidden = !on;
      });
      if (i === 1) drawMountain();
    };
    tabs.forEach((t, i) => {
      t.addEventListener("click", () => select(i));
      t.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
        if (e.key === "ArrowRight" || e.key === "ArrowLeft") {
          const n =
            (i + (e.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : tabs.length - 1)) % tabs.length;
          select(n);
          tabs[n].focus();
        }
      });
    });

    // ---------- simple fields ----------
    root
      .querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-k]")
      .forEach((el) => {
        el.value = state.f[el.dataset.k!] ?? "";
        el.addEventListener("input", () => {
          state.f[el.dataset.k!] = el.value;
          save();
          renderIntro();
        });
      });

    // ---------- 1. introduction ----------
    const introEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="intro"]')!;
    function renderIntro() {
      const f = state.f;
      const name = (f["m.name"] || "").trim();
      const parts: string[] = [];
      const clean = (s?: string) => (s || "").trim().replace(/\.$/, "");
      if (name) parts.push(`This is ${esc(name)} – my child.`);
      if (clean(f["m.mine"]))
        parts.push(
          `${name ? esc(name) : "My child"} carries something of me: ${esc(clean(f["m.mine"]))}.`,
        );
      if (clean(f["m.proud"]))
        parts.push(`I am proud of ${esc(clean(f["m.proud"]))}.`);
      if (clean(f["m.hope"]))
        parts.push(`For the future, I hope ${esc(clean(f["m.hope"]))}.`);
      if (clean(f["m.sorry"]))
        parts.push(
          `And if I am honest, I got one thing wrong: ${esc(clean(f["m.sorry"]))}. I am sorry for that.`,
        );
      introEl.innerHTML = parts.length
        ? "“" + parts.join(" ") + "”"
        : "Start typing, and her introduction will appear here.";
    }

    // ---------- 2. mountain ----------
    const stagesEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-stages]")!;
    const svg = root.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>("[data-mtn]")!;
    function renderStages() {
      stagesEl.innerHTML = state.stages
        .map(
          (s, i) => `
        <div class="stage">
          <span class="cn">C${i + 1}</span>
          <input type="text" aria-label="Name of stage ${i + 1}" placeholder="${i === 0 ? "e.g. Childhood" : i === state.stages.length - 1 ? "e.g. Today" : "Name this stage"}" value="${esc(s.name)}" data-i="${i}" data-f="name" />
          <label class="rng"><span>Low</span>
            <input type="range" min="1" max="10" value="${s.h}" aria-label="How high did stage ${i + 1} feel?" data-i="${i}" data-f="h" />
            <span>High</span></label>
          ${state.stages.length > 2 ? `<button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove stage ${i + 1}" data-rm="${i}">×</button>` : ""}
        </div>`,
        )
        .join("");
    }
    stagesEl.addEventListener("input", (e) => {
      const t = e.target as HTMLInputElement;
      const i = Number(t.dataset.i);
      if (Number.isNaN(i)) return;
      if (t.dataset.f === "name") state.stages[i].name = t.value;
      else state.stages[i].h = Number(t.value);
      save();
      drawMountain();
    });
    stagesEl.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>(
        "[data-rm]",
      );
      if (!b) return;
      state.stages.splice(Number(b.dataset.rm), 1);
      save();
      renderStages();
      drawMountain();
    });
    root.querySelector("[data-add-stage]")!.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (state.stages.length >= 8) return;
      state.stages.splice(state.stages.length - 1, 0, { name: "", h: 5 });
      save();
      renderStages();
      drawMountain();
    });

    function drawMountain() {
      const W = 720,
        H = 340,
        pad = 50,
        base = 300;
      const n = state.stages.length;
      const pts = state.stages.map((s, i) => [
        pad + (i * (W - 2 * pad)) / Math.max(1, n - 1),
        base - s.h * 20,
      ]);
      const line = pts.map((p) => p.join(" ")).join(" L ");
      const hi = pts.reduce((a, p, i) => (p[1] < pts[a][1] ? i : a), 0);
      const lo = pts.reduce((a, p, i) => (p[1] > pts[a][1] ? i : a), 0);
      const label = (s: Stage, i: number) =>
        esc(s.name || (i === 0 ? "Birth" : `Stage ${i + 1}`)).slice(0, 22);
      svg.innerHTML = `
        <rect width="${W}" height="${H}" fill="#fbe9e0"></rect>
        <circle cx="${W - 70}" cy="60" r="30" fill="#f2c6a8"></circle>
        <path d="M 0 ${base + 20} L ${line} L ${W} ${base + 20} L ${W} ${H} L 0 ${H} Z" fill="#0f5257"></path>
        <path d="M ${line}" fill="none" stroke="#e07a4f" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="7 7" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
        ${pts
          .map(
            (p, i) => `
          <circle cx="${p[0]}" cy="${p[1]}" r="7" fill="#f6f1ea"></circle>
          <text x="${p[0]}" y="${p[1] - 16}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="#12343b">C${i + 1}</text>
          <line x1="${p[0]}" y1="${p[1] + 8}" x2="${p[0]}" y2="${H - 34}" stroke="#f6f1ea" stroke-opacity="0.25" stroke-dasharray="2 4"></line><text x="${p[0]}" y="${H - 14}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#f6f1ea">${label(state.stages[i], i)}</text>`,
          )
          .join("")}
        ${n > 1 ? `<text x="${Math.min(W - 70, Math.max(70, pts[hi][0]))}" y="${pts[hi][1] - 36}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1" fill="#a94a22">THE PEAK</text>` : ""}
        ${n > 1 && lo !== hi ? `<text x="${Math.min(W - 90, Math.max(90, pts[lo][0]))}" y="${pts[lo][1] + 30}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1" fill="#f2c6a8">THE LOWEST POINT</text>` : ""}`;
    }

    // ---------- 3. values ----------
    const valuesEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-values]")!;
    const chipsEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="values"]')!;
    function renderValues() {
      valuesEl.innerHTML = state.values
        .map(
          (v, i) => `
        <div class="value">
          <input type="text" aria-label="Value ${i + 1}" placeholder="A value, e.g. honesty" value="${esc(v.name)}" data-i="${i}" data-f="name" />
          <select aria-label="Have you paid a price for value ${i + 1}?" data-i="${i}" data-f="paid">
            <option value="" ${v.paid === "" ? "selected" : ""}>Paid a price for it?</option>
            <option value="yes" ${v.paid === "yes" ? "selected" : ""}>Yes, I have</option>
            <option value="not-yet" ${v.paid === "not-yet" ? "selected" : ""}>Not yet</option>
            <option value="conflict" ${v.paid === "conflict" ? "selected" : ""}>It clashes with another value</option>
          </select>
          <input type="text" aria-label="When or how, for value ${i + 1}" placeholder="When, or how?" value="${esc(v.note)}" data-i="${i}" data-f="note" />
          ${state.values.length > 1 ? `<button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove value ${i + 1}" data-rm="${i}">×</button>` : ""}
        </div>`,
        )
        .join("");
      renderChips();
    }
    function renderChips() {
      const named = state.values.filter((v) => v.name.trim());
      chipsEl.innerHTML = named.length
        ? named
            .map(
              (v) =>
                `<span class="chip ${v.paid}">${esc(v.name.trim())}${v.paid === "yes" ? " ✓" : v.paid === "conflict" ? " ⇄" : ""}</span>`,
            )
            .join("") +
          `<p class="legend">✓ paid a price for it · ⇄ in conflict with another value</p>`
        : `<span class="muted">Your values will appear here.</span>`;
    }
    valuesEl.addEventListener("input", (e) => {
      const t = e.target as HTMLInputElement;
      const i = Number(t.dataset.i);
      if (Number.isNaN(i)) return;
      (state.values[i] as any)[t.dataset.f!] = t.value;
      save();
      renderChips();
    });
    valuesEl.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>(
        "[data-rm]",
      );
      if (!b) return;
      state.values.splice(Number(b.dataset.rm), 1);
      save();
      renderValues();
    });
    root.querySelector("[data-add-value]")!.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (state.values.length >= 6) return;
      state.values.push({ name: "", paid: "", note: "" });
      save();
      renderValues();
    });

    // ---------- footer ----------
    root.querySelector("[data-print]")!.addEventListener("click", () => {
      body.hidden = false;
      root
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[role="tabpanel"]')
        .forEach((p) => (p.hidden = false));
      drawMountain();
      document.body.classList.add("printing-kit");
      window.print();
      document.body.classList.remove("printing-kit");
      select(tabs.findIndex((t) => t.getAttribute("aria-selected") === "true"));
    });
    root.querySelector("[data-clear]")!.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (!confirm("Clear everything you have written in this exercise?"))
        return;
      state = blank();
      try {
        localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
      } catch {
        /* ignore */
      }
      root
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-k]")
        .forEach((el) => (el.value = ""));
      renderStages();
      renderValues();
      renderIntro();
      drawMountain();
    });

    renderStages();
    renderValues();
    renderIntro();
    drawMountain();
  }
</script>

<style is:global>
  .kit {
    margin: 3rem 0 2rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-top: 6px solid var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .kit-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .kit .kit-open {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .kit .kit-open[aria-expanded="true"] svg {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .kit .kit-body {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .kit .kit-body[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .kit-label {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .kit .kit-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    counter-increment: none;
  }

  .kit .kit-title::before {
    content: none;
  }

  .kit-intro,
  .kit .how {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .kit-privacy {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .kit .tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .kit [role="tab"] {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem 0.55rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .kit [role="tab"] span {
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--color-sand);
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .kit [role="tab"][aria-selected="true"] {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .kit [role="tab"][aria-selected="true"] span {
    background: var(--color-teal);
    color: var(--color-on-dark);
  }

  .kit .panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .kit .panel[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .kit .fields {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .kit .fields.two {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .kit label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .kit input[type="text"],
  .kit textarea,
  .kit select {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--color-ink, var(--color-primary));
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
    padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .kit textarea {
    resize: vertical;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .kit input:focus,
  .kit textarea:focus,
  .kit select:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .kit .out {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-teal);
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
  }

  .kit .out-label,
  .kit .prompt {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

